==============================================================================
PART A: tails make the pullback TWO-parameter (kappa-only fails);
        the single-a force prefactor survives; memory times; chords
==============================================================================
[A1] e.X' - (a/k^2)(cosh ks - 1) = 0
     With Z = H^2 X.X' and grad_1 Z = H^2 X' (tangential proj.):
     e.grad_1 W(Z) = W'(Z) * H^2 (e.X') = a * [H^2(cosh ks -1)/k^2] * W'(Z)
     => the force vertex carries EXACTLY ONE factor of a on the whole
        stationary family for ANY bi-invariant W(Z)  [tails included]:
        the deep-MOND consistency F -> 0 as a -> 0 survives for tails.
[A2] Z - [1 + 2(H/k)^2 sinh^2(ks/2)] = 0
     dZ/dH at FIXED kappa = 4*H*sinh(kappa*s/2)**2/kappa**2   != 0:
     => any NON-conformal W(Z) pulled back on the family knows (a,H)
        SEPARATELY: the agentF kappa-only lemma fails exactly here.
[A2] conformal exception: W_conf = H^2/(8pi^2(1-Z)) pulled back = -kappa**2/(8*pi**2*(cosh(kappa*s) - 1))   [H cancels: kappa-only — the Huygens accident]
[A2] conformal check of the A1 identity: (coshks-1)(H/k)^2 W' + W = 0   [=0 <=> e.gradW = -aW, agentF's identity recovered]
[A3] dS tail memory times: lambda_- = 3/2 - sqrt(9/4 - (m/H)^2);
     pullback decay rate lambda_-*kappa; T_mem = 1/(lambda_- kappa).
     m/H     lambda_-      m^2/3H^2     T_mem*H (kappa=H)
      0.03     0.000300     0.000300        3333.00
      0.10     0.003337     0.003333         299.67
      0.30     0.030306     0.030000          33.00
      1.00     0.381966     0.333333           2.62
      1.45     1.115943     0.700833           0.90
     [small m: lambda_- -> m^2/3H^2 (Starobinsky-Yokoyama rate m^2/3H);
      m -> 3H/2: T_mem -> (2/3)/H; principal series m > 3H/2: envelope
      rate 3kappa/2, oscillation mu*kappa, mu = sqrt(m^2/H^2 - 9/4) -> m:
      the kernel scale is the FIELD MASS once m >> H (flat-massive limit).
      => the dS-tail knee is bounded by ~max(m, H-class rates).]
[A4] Rindler chord^2 (t^2-x^2 sign: timelike>0): 0  [= (4/a^2)sinh^2(as/2):
     the massive tail J1(m*chord)/chord on the worldline depends on a
     EXPLICITLY — trajectory-dependent dissipation, as flagged by agentF]
[A4] helix chord^2 = s^2 * [1 + v^2*(1 - sin^2(Om s/2)/(Om s/2)^2) + O(v^4)]
     v^2 coefficient check: 0
     Sun's reflex helix: v = a/(Omega c) = 12.45 m/s -> v^2 = 1.72e-15:
     the straight-chord (flat-comoving) tail kernel is exact to ~1.7e-15
     on the solar worldline; galactic orbit v^2 ~ 6e-7: also negligible.
[A5] rhat.(r(t)-r(t-s)) - rho(1-cos Om s) = 0
     that.(r(t)-r(t-s)) - rho sin(Om s)   = 0
     => for an acceleration vector rotating at Omega, the tail force
        response per unit |a| is filtered by (1-cos Om s)/Om^2 (in-phase)
        and sin(Om s)/Om^2 (quadrature): Omega enters EXACTLY as the
        Fourier variable conjugate to memory time.  [rho = a/Omega^2]

