PART D: the memory quantum Langevin equation — structure and stability
==============================================================================
  Qdd + Om0^2 Q + lam^2 INT_0^inf [K_loc(s) + V(tau,tau-s)] Q(tau-s) ds
     = -lam phi_in(z(tau));   K_loc -> 2 gam Qd + dOm^2 Q, gam = lam^2/8pi
     (trajectory-BLIND, agentF lemma);  V = the tail: trajectory-DEPENDENT.
  Dressed internal propagator: h~(w) = 1/(Om_R^2 - w^2 - 2i gam w + lam^2 V~(w)).
  Flat-tail toy V~(w) = V0 (1 - e^{iwT})/(-iw),  V~(0) = V0*T = M0 (static).
[D1] zeros of the dressed denominator in the UPPER half-plane
     (Om_R=1, gam=0.05, T=20 i.e. knee 0.05; c_mem = lam^2 V0):
     c_mem = +0.02:  N_UHP = 0   STABLE
     c_mem = -0.02:  N_UHP = 0   STABLE
     c_mem = +0.20:  N_UHP = 2   UNSTABLE (2 pole(s) in UHP)
     c_mem = -0.20:  N_UHP = 1   UNSTABLE (1 pole(s) in UHP)
     c_mem = +1.00:  N_UHP = 2   UNSTABLE (2 pole(s) in UHP)
     c_mem = -1.00:  N_UHP = 1   UNSTABLE (1 pole(s) in UHP)
     [SHARP-cutoff toy: BOTH signs destabilize once |c_mem|*T ~ Om_R^2 —
      the abrupt kernel edge rings.  Smooth-kernel comparison below.]
[D2] smooth memory (exp kernel, V~(w) = c/(x - iw), x = 0.05): roots of
     the cubic (Om_R^2 - w^2 - 2i gam w)(x - iw) + c  [all must have Im<0]:
     c_mem = +0.200:  max Im(root) = +0.0466   UNSTABLE   [static dressed gap^2 = +5.00]
     c_mem = +1.000:  max Im(root) = +0.2915   UNSTABLE   [static dressed gap^2 = +21.00]
     c_mem = +4.000:  max Im(root) = +0.6397   UNSTABLE   [static dressed gap^2 = +81.00]
     c_mem = -0.020:  max Im(root) = -0.0300   STABLE   [static dressed gap^2 = +0.60]
     c_mem = -0.049:  max Im(root) = -0.0010   STABLE   [static dressed gap^2 = +0.02]
     c_mem = -0.051:  max Im(root) = +0.0010   UNSTABLE   [static dressed gap^2 = -0.02]
     c_mem = -0.200:  max Im(root) = +0.1433   UNSTABLE   [static dressed gap^2 = -3.00]
     c_mem = +0.090:  max Im(root) = -0.0052   STABLE   [passivity threshold 2gam(x^2+Om_R^2) = +0.100]
     c_mem = +0.110:  max Im(root) = +0.0045   UNSTABLE   [passivity threshold 2gam(x^2+Om_R^2) = +0.100]
     => TWO physical bounds, both machine-confirmed:
        (i) PASSIVITY: Im of the toy self-energy c w/(x^2+w^2) is anti-
        damping for c > 0; instability onsets at c = 2gam(x^2+Om_R^2)
        (bracketed at +0.09/+0.11 vs threshold 0.100): a PHYSICAL field
        tail must have Im(self-energy) <= 0 at w > 0 (radiation), which
        a real-positive pure-decay toy violates — the roots flag it.
        (ii) STATIC TACHYON: gap-REDUCING memory destabilizes exactly at
        Om_R^2 + V~(0) = 0 (bracketed at -0.049/-0.051): a memory-MOND
        (response-reducing) amplitude is bounded by stability.  Recorded;
        neither bound touches the worldline-inertia gate of Part E.

