  - tails: dissipation kernel = trajectory-dependent memory ([A2],[A4]);
    single-a prefactor survives ([A1]); kappa-only census premise FAILS
  - dS m=0 minimal tail = constant H^2/4pi inside the cone ([B]): the
    flat-tail toy is exact; endpoint V(0+) = -(1/8pi)[m^2+(xi-1/6)R] ([C])
  - memory Langevin: smooth memory stable up to the static-tachyon point
    (gap-reducing amplitude bounded by stability); sharp-cutoff toy rings ([D])
  - helix filters: m_R(0) = INT K s^2/2 (LOCAL, analytic in Om^2 — the
    standard quasi-static localization, full weight); gate m_R -> M0/Om^2:
    p = 2 UNIVERSAL (sharp AND smooth kernels); m_T -> K(0)/Om^3: p = 3;
    moment expansion valid slow, fails fast, response averaged out ([E])
  - window for the knee: [2.0e-14, 2.5e-9] s^-1 (framework, conservative)
    [2.0e-14, 4.0e-10] (hostile): NON-EMPTY, 4.3-5.1 decades;
    mc^2 ~ [1.3e-29, 1.6e-24] eV; T_mem ~ decades..1.6 Myr ([F])
  - the PURE-dS tail (knee <= 3H/2) misses the window by ~3.9 decades,
    tilts the RAR by ~4.9 dex, overdrives clusters x1000: EXCLUDED ([F6])
